@native
@label "Entries"
@description "Convert a record into a list of {key, value} pairs. ∀a. Record String a → List {key: String, value: a}. Phase 13a-1: enables Fenel-side iteration over Record<String, _> shapes (handleList expansion in profiles, applyMapping in imports) — previously kept wrapper-side TS because std lacked entries/keys/values primitives."
@tags "record" "iteration"
entries : (record: {  }) -> List ({ key: String, value: a })

@native
@label "From entries"
@description "The O(n) inverse of `entries`: build a record from a list of {key, value} pairs in ONE pass. ∀a. List {key: String, value: a} → Record String a. FIRST occurrence of a key wins (a later duplicate is dropped) — mirrors a first-match assoc-list lookup. parser-substrate 7h S2: the opaque-map perf branch — folding an index with the immutable-spread `mapSet` is O(n²), so this builds the lookup index O(n) for the parser's env (the pure assoc-list stays the source of truth; this is the JS-object index perf rep)."
@tags "record" "iteration" "parser-substrate" "phase-7h"
fromEntries : (pairs: List ({ key: String, value: a })) -> {  }

@native
@label "Map get"
@description "Read a record field by a DYNAMIC string key, returning Maybe (Just value when the key is present, Nothing when absent). ∀a. Record String a → String → Maybe a. The O(1) READ sibling of `mapSet` — genuinely inexpressible in a `.fenel` body because `.field` access is static-keyed. parser-substrate 7h S2: the opaque-map perf branch that makes the parser's env lookups (findEntry/lookupBool/lookupVal/bodyOf) constant-time over a `fromEntries`-built index; the pure assoc-list stays the source of truth."
@tags "record" "lookup" "parser-substrate" "phase-7h"
mapGet : (record: {  }) -> (key: String) -> Maybe a

@native
@label "Evaluate expression"
@description "Evaluate a stored JSON-Logic expression-value against a data record — the engine's own `evaluate` surfaced reflectively to a Fenel body (expression-as-runtime-value, design/expression-mobility-and-policy.md). NOT a new dialect: it IS the canonical evaluator, made Fenel-callable. Uses the default (EMPTY_CTX) evaluate — built-in ops + `var` reads only, no user-function dispatch — which is exact parity with the form-submit wrapper's `evaluate(expr, data)`. Pure (deterministic, no IO). The stored expr stays inert data until this call (the body reaches it only via a `var` read), so passing JSON-Logic through a body's params is safe without quoting. Added in Phase 5a-submit of the ts-elimination-completion workstream — the form-trigger / on-submit-rule condition evaluator the loops fold over."
@tags "eval" "json-logic" "expression-mobility" "phase-5a"
evalExpr : (expr: {  }) -> (data: {  }) -> a

@native
@label "Format template"
@description "Substitute `{name}` placeholders in a template string with values pulled from the args record. Missing keys leave the placeholder in place. Substitution is shallow — nested objects are coerced to a JSON-ish string."
@tags "text" "template" "interpolation"
format : (template: String) -> (args: {  }) -> String

