@description "Parse a JSON-text string into a List of records: `JSON.parse(s)`, then array-coerce (a top-level array passes through; a single object is wrapped to a one-element list). Irreducible host-marshalling leaf — arbitrary-JSON-text parsing has no reasonable pure-Fenel form (same bridge class as the host-string leaves urlEncode / regexSet). Pure (deterministic, no IO). Throws on malformed JSON (parity with the wrapper-side `JSON.parse` it replaces). Added in Phase 5a-csv of the ts-elimination-completion workstream — the JSON fork of imports:parseRows."
@tags "parse" "json" "input"
